## Backend Changes (FastAPI)

### New Router: `routers/resume_builder.py`

| Endpoint | Method | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `/builder/extract` | POST | Upload PDF or text → AI extracts achievements → returns list for verification |
| `/builder/achievements` | GET | List all achievements for the authenticated user |
| `/builder/achievements` | POST | Manually add a new achievement |
| `/builder/achievements/{id}` | PATCH | Edit an existing achievement |
| `/builder/achievements/{id}` | DELETE | Delete an achievement |
| `/builder/generate` | POST | Given `achievement_id` + `target_role` → generate 3-5 bullet variants using placement-tier RAG |
| `/builder/save-bullet` | POST | Save a generated bullet to the Point Bank |
| `/builder/point-bank` | GET | Get all saved bullets for the user, grouped by role |
| `/builder/point-bank/{id}` | DELETE | Remove a bullet from the Point Bank |
| `/builder/strategy` | POST | Given `target_role` + user's vault → return gap analysis + recommendations |
| `/builder/reconstruct` | POST | Metric reconstruction chat turn (achievement_id + conversation history → AI asks targeted metric questions) |

### New Agent: `agents/achievement_engine.py`

Core logic for:
1. **`extract_achievements(text, source_type)`** — Gemini extracts individual achievements from resume text or raw notes. Returns structured JSON with title, description, competency tags, metrics, confidence.
2. **`generate_bullet_variants(achievement, target_role, golden_context)`** — Given a structured achievement + RAG context from placement-tier golden examples, generate 3-5 role-specific bullet variants with scoring.
3. **`generate_strategy(achievements, target_role)`** — Analyze the full vault against successful placement profiles, identify strengths/gaps, recommend which achievements to prioritize.
4. **`reconstruct_metrics(achievement, chat_history)`** — Interactive metric reconstruction: AI asks targeted questions based on the achievement context to help the user quantify their impact.

### New Script: `scripts/ingest_placement_resumes.py`

A script modeled on the existing `process_casebooks.py` but designed for senior placement resumes:
- Input: PDF files in `data/resumes/placement/` organized by domain subfolder
- Pipeline: Parse PDF → Extract bullets → Classify by competency tags → Embed → Upsert into `golden_resume_bullets` with `tier='placement'`
- Supports metadata: domain, company (from filename convention), tier

